我巴不得它把法拉利脸上的得瑟笑容给彻底抹掉。
I want it to wipe the smile
off Ferrari's face.

274
00:14:33,700 --> 00:14:35,367
众人：好！
ALL: Yeah!

275
00:14:35,367 --> 00:14:37,733
-（观众鼓掌）
-实际上，这就是这台车该背负的使命。
-(APPLAUDING)
-In fact, that should
be this car's mission.

276
00:14:37,767 --> 00:14:40,233
从今往后它就这一个用处了。必须的。
That's all it's for
from now on. Definitely.

277
00:14:40,267 --> 00:14:44,133
好了，每周我们都会收到小朋友发来的邮件和信件，
问我们：
Right, now, every week
we get emails and letters
from children asking

278
00:14:44,167 --> 00:14:46,833
“世界上最疯癫的车是哪台？”
"Which is the craziest car
in the world?"

279
00:14:46,867 --> 00:14:49,267
嗯，这听上去还挺像个挑战的。
Well, that sounded like
a bit of a challenge.

280
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:55,367
可能大家会觉得，
要找最疯癫的车得去日本，
Now,
you might think Japan
to find the maddest cars,

281
00:14:55,367 --> 00:14:57,267
或者是美国，但并不是。
or America, but no.

282
00:14:57,367 --> 00:15:01,567
你得来这片欧洲疯狂思想的温床——
瑞士。
You have to come
to that hotbed of European
craziness, Switzerland.

283
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:04,600
这倒挺奇怪的，
因为瑞士人对汽车向来不太感冒。
And that's a bit odd
because the Swiss
aren't big on cars.

284
00:15:04,633 --> 00:15:06,500
他们压根没有自己的汽车工业，
They don't have
a motor industry

285
00:15:06,533 --> 00:15:08,900
甚至还不允许赛车运动，
and they don't even
allow motorsport

286
00:15:08,933 --> 00:15:10,600
生怕有人开得太快。
in case someone goes to fast.

287
00:15:14,733 --> 00:15:18,767
尽管如此，
这地方却压抑着某种对汽车的狂热，
Despite all that,
there is some pent-up
car passion in this place,

288
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:22,233
而且时不时地，
就像火山爆发一样喷涌而出。
and every so often,
like a volcano, it goes off.

289
00:15:22,267 --> 00:15:24,900
（摇滚乐响起）
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

290
00:15:32,067 --> 00:15:33,800
这就是“贝都因人”（Bedouin）。
This is the Bedouin.

291
00:15:33,833 --> 00:15:37,400
它是瑞士林斯比得（Rinspeed）公司的杰作，
这家公司专门……
It's the creation of Rinspeed,
a Swiss company
that specialises

292
00:15:37,433 --> 00:15:42,200
专门为全世界腰缠万贯的车迷
定制孤品豪车。
in making one-off cars
for well-heeled petrolheads
all over the world.

293
00:15:44,433 --> 00:15:46,433
它最初只是一辆保时捷911，
It started out as a 911,

294
00:15:46,467 --> 00:15:51,067
然后就被魔改成了一件
价值三十万英镑的范思哲大牌货。
and then it was turned into
a sort of £300,000 Versace.

295
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:55,867
不过因为配了双涡轮增压，
它零到六十英里加速依然能跑进六秒之内。
But because it's got
twin turbos, it'll still do
0-60 in under six seconds.

296
00:15:57,800 --> 00:15:59,133
（轻笑）
(CHUCKLES)

297
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:02,867
妙极了。
Fabulous.

298
00:16:04,900 --> 00:16:09,100
但我能感觉得出，你们还想要
更多一点的超现实主义。
But I can sense you're wanting
a little more surrealism.

299
00:16:09,133 --> 00:16:10,833
那咱们就来看看细节吧，如何？
So let's look at
the details, shall we?

300
00:16:14,667 --> 00:16:19,200
这个挡把绝非你在哈福德百货
花两镑九毛九买的“拉力特配款”。
The gear knob is none
of your Halfords
£2.99 rally special jobs.

301
00:16:19,233 --> 00:16:21,400
哦，才不是，这玩意儿是水晶的。
Oh, no. This one is crystal.

302
00:16:21,433 --> 00:16:25,567
事实上，整套内饰
可不只是裹上了奢华真皮，
And in fact, the whole
of the interior isn't just
clad in sumptuous leather.

303
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:30,600
更是豪横地镶满了施华洛世奇水晶。
真讲究。
It is liberally swathed
in Swarovski crystal. Nice.

304
00:16:30,633 --> 00:16:34,667
不妨把它当成某种
瑞士保时捷版的“利伯拉契”。
Think of it as a kind of
Swiss Porsche Liberace.

305
00:16:34,700 --> 00:16:38,267
但好戏还没完呢，
哦，并没有，因为它还能搞这个。
But the fun isn't over yet,
oh, no, because it does this.

306
00:16:41,867 --> 00:16:46,200
这大概是全世界
设计最繁琐、最过度工程化的后备箱盖了。
Possibly, the most
over-engineered
boot lid in the world.

307
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:55,367
林斯比得的工厂
深藏在瑞士的崇山峻岭中，
The Rinspeed workshops
are hidden away
in the Swiss mountains,

308
00:16:55,400 --> 00:16:58,733
外面还有夺命杀手奶牛把守。
where they are guarded
by killer cows.

309
00:17:00,267 --> 00:17:05,367
在这座秘密老巢里，
诞生了一台台光怪陆离的奇葩机器。
And inside the lair,
strange and wondrous
machines are created.

310
00:17:07,567 --> 00:17:10,500
感觉就像是007里的Q博士
被邦德的反派给绑架了，
It's as though Q has
been hijacked by the
Bond baddies

311
00:17:10,533 --> 00:17:13,067
然后被押到山里的秘密实验室打黑工。
and put to work in
secret labs in the mountains.

312
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:14,500
搞出来的成果简直绝了。
And the results are amazing.

313
00:17:14,533 --> 00:17:17,667
这玩意儿烧天然气，
而且车身中间还能倾斜。
This thing runs on gas and
kind of tilts in the middle.

314
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:20,167
那台后面背了一艘气垫船。
That one has got
a hovercraft on the back.

315
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:22,700
至于那一台……
可千万别让我开口吐槽。
And that one,
don't even get me started.

316
00:17:22,733 --> 00:17:24,467
而眼前这一台，绝对值得一瞧。
And this is well worth a look.

317
00:17:32,467 --> 00:17:33,533
“急板”（Presto）。
The Presto.

318
00:17:33,567 --> 00:17:35,633
它是基于奔驰A级打造的。
It's based on
a Mercedes A-Class.

319
00:17:35,667 --> 00:17:37,867
我懂，这底子听着确实不怎么让人提得起劲。
I know, not the most
exciting of starts.

320
00:17:37,900 --> 00:17:41,133
它的尾灯确实设计得很巧妙，但……切，有什么好得瑟的。
It does have clever
tail lamps, but whoopee-do.

321
00:17:41,167 --> 00:17:43,000
但它还有另一项绝活。
But it does have
another trick.

322
00:17:43,033 --> 00:17:46,033
你看，我觉得瑞士这地方
停车肯定是个老大难，
You see, I think there must
be a bit of parking problem
in Switzerland,

323
00:17:46,067 --> 00:17:48,233
因为这是一辆
四座敞篷跑车。
because this is
a four-seater roadster.

324
00:17:48,267 --> 00:17:50,133
车身还挺长的。
It's quite long.

325
00:17:50,167 --> 00:17:51,767
但只要按一下按钮……
But at the touch
of a button...

326
00:17:58,667 --> 00:18:00,467
这确实有点厉害。
That is impressive.

327
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:03,733
但别忘了，我们要找的
是能找到的最离谱的车。
But remember, we're looking
for the maddest car
we can find.

328
00:18:03,767 --> 00:18:05,233
所以，继续出发！
So, onward!

329
00:18:15,133 --> 00:18:17,667
接下来这辆，我认为
And so we come
to what is, I think,

330
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:21,833
堪称奇葩车界里的终极圣杯。
the Holy Grail of cars
that are just out there.

331
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:25,933
这位是弗莱迪，他是瑞士人。
This is Freddy. He's Swiss.

332
00:18:25,967 --> 00:18:27,367
他必须得陪着我，
He has to be with me

333
00:18:27,367 --> 00:18:29,833
原因我待会儿再解释。
for reasons I shall
explain in a moment.

334
00:18:31,867 --> 00:18:35,600
这辆车装了一台
雪地摩托的750cc发动机。
This car has a 750cc engine
from a snowmobile.

335
00:18:35,633 --> 00:18:38,533
这挺有意思，
但还算不上惊人。
And that's interesting,
but not amazing.

336
00:18:40,367 --> 00:18:43,600
它的造价将近90万英镑，
It would cost you
just under £900,000,

337
00:18:43,633 --> 00:18:45,867
虽说这价格确实挺吓人的，
and while that is
pretty astonishing,

338
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:47,933
但重头戏还没到呢。
we're not quite there yet.

339
00:18:47,967 --> 00:18:52,500
那么，它到底有什么魔力，
值得我们大老远跑来看它？
So, what is it about this car
that makes it the one
we've come to see?

340
00:18:56,467 --> 00:19:00,433
它叫Splash（水花），这名字就给了提示，
Well, it's called the Splash,
and there's a clue,

341
00:19:02,467 --> 00:19:06,867
因为这是全世界
第一辆水翼汽车。
because this is the world's
first hydrofoil car.

342
00:19:15,367 --> 00:19:18,367
后扰流板向下折叠。
The rear spoiler folds down.

343
00:19:18,367 --> 00:19:22,000
两侧的翼板也展开并翻折出来。
Other spoilers deploy
from the side and fold out.

344
00:19:22,033 --> 00:19:23,400
然后突然之间……
And all of a sudden...

345
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:26,367
（声音含混不清）
(INDISTINCT)

346
00:19:27,367 --> 00:19:31,433
我们飞起来了！
在水上飞！坐在一辆车里！
We're flying!
On the water. In a car.

347
00:19:31,467 --> 00:19:32,533
太爽了！
Yes!

348
00:19:38,233 --> 00:19:41,133
我快吓尿了，
但又莫名觉得刺激！
I'm scared,
but strangely thrilled!

349
00:19:47,467 --> 00:19:50,067
虽说折腾了几回，
So, it took a few attempts,

350
00:19:50,100 --> 00:19:52,067
我还特地大老远跑来瑞士。
I had to come to Switzerland.

351
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:54,033
但我觉得我们总算是成了。
But I think
we've finally done it.

352
00:19:54,067 --> 00:19:55,800
我们找到了这辆
We've found what is got to be

353
00:19:55,833 --> 00:19:58,167
绝对算得上全世界最疯狂的车。
the maddest car in the world.

354
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:02,533
（观众鼓掌）
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

355
00:20:02,567 --> 00:20:03,733
克拉克森：相当精彩！
CLARKSON: Very good!

356
00:20:06,900 --> 00:20:09,200
九十万英镑……
£900,000...

357
00:20:09,233 --> 00:20:10,767
噢，没错，确实是。
Oh, yes. Yes.

358
00:20:10,800 --> 00:20:13,267
-而且它就像是
船、车和飞机的合体。
-能飞的飞机，没错。
-And it's a sort
of boat-car-plane.
-Flying plane, yeah.

359
00:20:13,367 --> 00:20:15,000
所以我认为
这是史上最离谱的车。
And therefore I think
the craziest car ever.

360
00:20:15,033 --> 00:20:18,100
当然，除非你们知道更疯的，
要是知道就告诉我们。
Unless, of course,
you know any better,
in which case let us know.

361
00:20:18,133 --> 00:20:21,067
没错，不过现在又到了
Absolutely, but now it
is time to put a star

362
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:22,900
“廉价车请名人”环节了。
in our reasonably-priced car.

363
00:20:22,933 --> 00:20:24,833
女士们先生们，
乔安娜·拉姆利！
Ladies and gentlemen,
Joanna Lumley!

364
00:20:24,867 --> 00:20:26,367
（全场欢呼）
(ALL CHEERING)

365
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:29,900
-嗨，你好吗？
-我挺好的。
-Hi, there. How are you?
-I'm good.

366
00:20:30,867 --> 00:20:31,867
-请坐。
-谢谢。
-Have a seat.
-Thank you.

367
00:20:36,700 --> 00:20:38,267
能请到你真是蓬荜生辉。
Now, this is an honour.

368
00:20:38,367 --> 00:20:40,733
你能来我们这儿，
绝对是莫大的荣幸，
真的。
This is a proper honour
to have you here.
It really is.

369
00:20:40,767 --> 00:20:42,900
我太激动了，
我每周都看你们节目。
I'm so thrilled.
I watch this every week.

370
00:20:42,933 --> 00:20:43,967
-真的假的？
-真的。
-You do?
-Yeah.

371
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,467
-你居然还是这节目的粉丝？
-是啊。
-You're even a fan
of the show?
-Yeah.

372
00:20:45,500 --> 00:20:47,067
周日晚上反正也没别的可看。
What else is on Sunday night?

373
00:20:47,100 --> 00:20:49,833
坦白说，大多数人都能找到
比我们更有营养的节目看。
Most people can find
something better
to watch, frankly.

374
00:20:49,867 --> 00:20:52,600
呃，问题是，
你听起来像个蓝血贵族。
Um, now the thing is that
you sound like a blue-blood.

375
00:20:52,633 --> 00:20:54,500
-没错。
-但我研究了一下你的底细，
-Yeah.
-But I've been reading
up on you,

376
00:20:54,533 --> 00:20:56,833
感觉你那血管里
流淌的没准全都是汽油。
and it sounds like there
might be a bit of petrol
going on in those veins.

377
00:20:56,867 --> 00:20:58,467
-流着呢，汩汩流淌着。
-真的？
-It's there.
It's running through.
-Really?

378
00:20:58,500 --> 00:21:00,833
打从……对啊，
打我记事起，我就喜欢……
Ever since, yeah...
Ever since, I can remember,
I liked...

379
00:21:00,867 --> 00:21:02,367
比起洋娃娃我更喜欢汽车。
I liked cars above dolls.

380
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:04,800
我小时候还搭过一个小车库呢。
I used to have a little garage
when I was young.

381
00:21:04,833 --> 00:21:07,667
而且到现在我还留着
一堆铁皮小玩具车。
And I've still got
a collection
of little tin cars.

382
00:21:07,700 --> 00:21:10,233
你的第一段“风流韵事”
是跟一辆劳斯莱斯？
Your first love affair
was with a Rolls-Royce.

383
00:21:10,267 --> 00:21:11,667
-对。
-怎么说？
-Yeah.
-Why is that?

384
00:21:11,700 --> 00:21:13,733
因为当时有人敲我门说：
Because somebody knocked
on the door and said,

385
00:21:13,767 --> 00:21:15,667
“乔安娜，外头有辆车”，
你懂的。
"Joanna, there's
a car outside,"
you know.

386
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:17,067
“只要550，你要不要下楼瞧瞧？”
"It's 550, do you
want to look down?"

387
00:21:17,100 --> 00:21:18,467
我往窗外一瞅，直接……（倒吸气）
I looked out the window
and went... (GASPS)

388
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:20,867
“那是辆劳斯莱斯啊！”
他说：“对啊，才550块。”
"It's a Rolls-Royce!"
And he said, "Yeah, just 550."

389
00:21:20,900 --> 00:21:22,367
550英镑？对。
£550? Yeah.

390
00:21:22,367 --> 00:21:24,700
那车漂亮极了。
是辆1949年的银魂，
She was peachy.
It was a Silver Wraith, 1949,

391
00:21:24,733 --> 00:21:27,400
带着登车踏板，
还有大号的卢卡斯车灯。
with running boards and
big Lucas headlamps.

392
00:21:27,433 --> 00:21:29,333
而且它还有，呃，那种雨刮器，
And it had, um,
windscreen wipers

393
00:21:29,367 --> 00:21:33,733
你得两只手都离开方向盘，
像这样去拧开它。
that you had to take
both your hands off the wheel
and start them, like that.

394
00:21:33,767 --> 00:21:36,267
真有创意的设计。
真奇怪这设计居然没流行开来。
An interesting idea.
I'm surprised that
didn't catch on.

395
00:21:36,300 --> 00:21:37,667
而且那车门是反向开的，
And the doors opened
like that,

396
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:39,500
所以有时候如果我没关严实，
so, sometimes
if I hadn't shut it properly,

397
00:21:39,533 --> 00:21:41,333
它们就会猛地弹开，顺带把骑自行车的扫飞。
they'd fly open
and take a cyclist away.

398
00:21:42,367 --> 00:21:44,033
不过话说回来……倒也挺管用，
But then...
They're quite useful,

399
00:21:44,067 --> 00:21:45,867
毕竟你正经上过
露西·克莱顿名媛仪态学校。
'cause you did
the whole Lucie Clayton
finishing school thing.

400
00:21:45,900 --> 00:21:48,133
-对。
-专门学怎么优雅地上下车。
-Yeah.
-About how to get in
and out of cars.

401
00:21:48,167 --> 00:21:50,633
没错，双腿并拢。
微笑，递手。谢谢。
Yes, knees together.
Smile, hand. Thank you.

402
00:21:51,367 --> 00:21:53,200
就那一套。端端正正坐着。
All that. Sitting like that.

403
00:21:53,233 --> 00:21:55,300
但你确实学过怎么优雅下车
才不至于露底走光，对吧？
But you do learn
how to get out without showing
your knickers, don't you?

404
00:21:55,333 --> 00:21:58,367
没错，必须学。因为他们总以为
带你出去约会的男人
开的都是捷豹E-Type。
Yes, you have to. 'Cause they
always think you're gonna be
taken out in an E-type Jag.

405
00:21:58,400 --> 00:22:01,467
但你当然从来就没交过
买得起捷豹E-Type的男朋友。从来没有。
And of course you never have
a boyfriend who's got an
E-type Jaguar. Never.

406
00:22:01,500 --> 00:22:03,333
你知道的，我那些男朋友
出门全靠挤地铁。
You know, they go by Tube,
my boyfriends.

407
00:22:03,367 --> 00:22:05,633
-（大笑）
-所以学那套挺辛酸的，纯属浪费时间。
-(LAUGHS)
-So that was a bit sad
and a waste of time.

408
00:22:05,667 --> 00:22:07,467
而且我也不想就那么干坐着。
And also I didn't want
